id=a52sxq_pif_stack_removal
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: remove the ROM's Play Integrity stack (one-time cleanup)
author=kusti420
Since 9.3.101 the ROM is back on the 9.3.88 setup (framework PlayIntegrityHooks + KeyboxImitationHooks, unica/mods/pif and unica/mods/keybox, with their Settings pages; owner 2026-11-03); the module stack of 9.3.92-9.3.97 stays removed. This patch replaces pif_stack (Zygisk Next, TEESimulator, PIF, k4-gmscompat, shipped keybox, Settings keybox/PIF pages). On phones updated from a build that had it, /system/bin/k4-pif-cleanup runs once after boot (KernelSU's domain) and removes what that stack left in /data, touching nothing the user installed or changed: modules k4-gmscompat installed (its /data/adb/.k4_gmscompat/<id>.ours) still at that versionCode are uninstalled with ksud (gone from the next boot) - Zygisk Next only when no other active module still has a zygisk/ library -, the configs it seeded (/data/adb/pif.prop, /data/adb/teesim/{config,overrides}.json) and the shipped keybox are deleted when byte-identical to what was shipped and their module is gone (/data/adb/teesim is emptied when the ROM-installed TEESimulator goes, except a keybox.xml that is not the shipped one) (the Settings keybox import, Settings.Secure unica_keybox_data, and the persist.sys.unica.{pif,keybox} switches are left alone: they belong to the framework hooks again). Two boots: ksud only marks modules for removal and a still-running TEESimulator rewrites its files, so the file cleanup (and the state dir) waits for the boot on which the uninstalled modules are gone (sys.k4.pifcleanup pending:... -> done:...). Result in sys.k4.pifcleanup, log in the kernel log.
